{"id":"code-evaluate","title":"Integer expression evaluator","category":"code","difficulty":5,"prompt":"Write a Python function `evaluate(expression: str) -> int` that evaluates an integer\narithmetic expression without using `eval`, `exec` or `ast`.\n\n- Tokens: non-negative integer literals, the binary operators + - * /, unary minus,\n  parentheses, and spaces (which are ignored between tokens).\n- Precedence is the usual one: unary minus binds tightest, then * and /, then + and -.\n  Binary operators are left-associative. Unary minus may be repeated (\"--4\" is 4).\n- `/` is integer division that truncates toward zero: 7 / 2 is 3 and -7 / 2 is -3.\n- Dividing by zero raises ZeroDivisionError.\n- Any malformed expression, including an empty one or an unsupported operator, raises\n  ValueError.","system":"You are completing one task from an evaluation suite. Do the task as asked.\n\nReply with one Python code block that defines exactly what the task asks for. Use only the standard library. Do not include tests, examples, or print statements.","grader":{"type":"code","entrypoint":"evaluate","tests":["assert evaluate(\"1 + 2 * 3\") == 7","assert evaluate(\"(1 + 2) * 3\") == 9","assert evaluate(\"  42  \") == 42","assert evaluate(\"2 - 3 - 4\") == -5","assert evaluate(\"2 * (3 + 4) * 5\") == 70","assert evaluate(\"7 / 2\") == 3","assert evaluate(\"-7 / 2\") == -3","assert evaluate(\"7 / -2\") == -3","assert evaluate(\"-7 / -2\") == 3","assert evaluate(\"10 / 3 / 2\") == 1","assert evaluate(\"-(2 + 3)\") == -5","assert evaluate(\"2 * -3\") == -6","assert evaluate(\"--4\") == 4","assert raises(ZeroDivisionError, evaluate, \"8 / (3 - 3)\")","assert raises(ValueError, evaluate, \"2 +\")","assert raises(ValueError, evaluate, \"(1 + 2\")","assert raises(ValueError, evaluate, \"2 ** 3\")","assert raises(ValueError, evaluate, \"\")","assert raises(ValueError, evaluate, \"1 2\")","assert raises(ValueError, evaluate, \"2 x 3\")"]},"reference":"```python\ndef evaluate(expression: str) -> int:\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(expression):\n        ch = expression[i]\n        if ch == \" \":\n            i += 1\n        elif ch.isdigit():\n            j = i\n            while j < len(expression) and expression[j].isdigit():\n                j += 1\n            tokens.append(int(expression[i:j]))\n            i = j\n        elif ch in \"+-*/()\":\n            tokens.append(ch)\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unexpected character {ch!r}\")\n    pos = 0\n\n    def peek():\n        return tokens[pos] if pos < len(tokens) else None\n\n    def take():\n        nonlocal pos\n        pos += 1\n        return tokens[pos - 1]\n\n    def factor() -> int:\n        token = peek()\n        if token == \"-\":\n            take()\n            return -factor()\n        if token == \"(\":\n            take()\n            value = expr()\n            if peek() != \")\":\n                raise ValueError(\"missing closing parenthesis\")\n            take()\n            return value\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            return take()\n        raise ValueError(\"expected a number\")\n\n    def term() -> int:\n        value = factor()\n        while peek() in (\"*\", \"/\"):\n            op = take()\n            right = factor()\n            if op == \"*\":\n                value *= right\n            else:\n                if right == 0:\n                    raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")\n                quotient = abs(value) // abs(right)\n                value = quotient if (value >= 0) == (right >= 0) else -quotient\n        return value\n\n    def expr() -> int:\n        value = term()\n        while peek() in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n            op = take()\n            right = term()\n            value = value + right if op == \"+\" else value - right\n        return value\n\n    result = expr()\n    if pos != len(tokens):\n        raise ValueError(\"unexpected trailing input\")\n    return result\n```","answers":["```python\nimport re\n\ndef evaluate(expression: str) -> int:\n    if not re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9+\\-*/() ]+\", expression):\n        raise ValueError(\"unsupported character\")\n    try:\n        return int(eval(expression.replace(\"/\", \"//\")))\n    except SyntaxError as error:\n        raise ValueError(str(error)) from error\n```","```python\ndef evaluate(expression: str) -> int:\n    tokens = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(expression):\n        ch = expression[i]\n        if ch == \" \":\n            i += 1\n        elif ch.isdigit():\n            j = i\n            while j < len(expression) and expression[j].isdigit():\n                j += 1\n            tokens.append(int(expression[i:j]))\n            i = j\n        elif ch in \"+-*/()\":\n            tokens.append(ch)\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            raise ValueError(f\"unexpected character {ch!r}\")\n    pos = 0\n\n    def peek():\n        return tokens[pos] if pos < len(tokens) else None\n\n    def take():\n        nonlocal pos\n        pos += 1\n        return tokens[pos - 1]\n\n    def factor() -> int:\n        token = peek()\n        if token == \"-\":\n            take()\n            return -factor()\n        if token == \"(\":\n            take()\n            value = expr()\n            if peek() != \")\":\n                raise ValueError(\"missing closing parenthesis\")\n            take()\n            return value\n        if isinstance(token, int):\n            return take()\n        raise ValueError(\"expected a number\")\n\n    def term() -> int:\n        value = factor()\n        while peek() in (\"*\", \"/\"):\n            op = take()\n            right = factor()\n            if op == \"*\":\n                value *= right\n            else:\n                if right == 0:\n                    raise ZeroDivisionError(\"division by zero\")\n                quotient = abs(value) // abs(right)\n                value = quotient if (value >= 0) == (right >= 0) else -quotient\n        return value\n\n    def expr() -> int:\n        value = term()\n        while peek() in (\"+\", \"-\"):\n            op = take()\n            right = term()\n            value = value + right if op == \"+\" else value - right\n        return value\n\n    result = expr()\n    if pos != len(tokens):\n        raise ValueError(\"unexpected trailing input\")\n    return result\n```"],"cells":[{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":0,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.85,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":17,"total":20,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.02,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":278,"output_tokens":364,"cost_usd":0.0002098,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":1,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.85,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":17,"total":20,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true}],"simulated":{"pass_probability":0.02,"answer":"known-wrong"}},"input_tokens":278,"output_tokens":598,"cost_usd":0.0003268,"latency_ms":null},{"arm":"haiku-low","trial":2,"mode":"batch","status":"ok","score":0.85,"passed":false,"answer":0,"details":{"passed":17,"total":20,"tests":[{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":false,"error":"AssertionError"},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":true},{"ok":tr